### Expense Tracker API — example requests
### Compatible with the VS Code REST Client extension and the JetBrains HTTP client.
###
### Workflow:
###   1. Run "Register" or "Login". The response sets a `token` cookie that
###      subsequent requests reuse automatically.
###   2. Run "Create a category", "Add a budget", etc. in order.
###   3. Replace the @cat_id / @raw_id variables with values returned by earlier requests.

@host = http://localhost:8000
@email = demo@example.com
@password = correct-horse-battery-staple

### Health check (no auth required)
GET {{host}}/health

###

### Register — sets `token` cookie + returns access_token
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###

### Login — sets `token` cookie + returns access_token
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###

### Who am I?
GET {{host}}/auth/me

###

### Create a category
POST {{host}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "groceries" }

###

### List categories
GET {{host}}/categories

###

### Create a budget for a year (replace category_id with one from the list above)
@cat_id = REPLACE_WITH_CATEGORY_UUID

POST {{host}}/budget
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "year": 2026,
  "entries": [
    { "category_id": "{{cat_id}}", "allocated_amount": 60000 }
  ]
}

###

### Get this year's budget
GET {{host}}/budget/2026

###

### Add a person to split with
POST {{host}}/persons
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "alex" }

###

### Add a tag
POST {{host}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "work-reimbursable" }

###

### List raw transactions
GET {{host}}/transactions/raw

###

### Manually add a raw transaction (skip the PDF for now)
POST {{host}}/transactions/raw
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "txn_date": "2026-05-12",
  "description": "BLINKIT BANGALORE",
  "amount": 480.50
}

###

### Auto-categorise pending raw rows
POST {{host}}/transactions/auto-categorise
Content-Type: application/json

{ "save_mapping": false }

###

### Manually process one raw row (use a raw_txn_id from the list above)
@raw_id = REPLACE_WITH_RAW_TXN_UUID
@person_id = REPLACE_WITH_PERSON_UUID

POST {{host}}/transactions/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "raw_txn_id": "{{raw_id}}",
  "category_id": "{{cat_id}}",
  "tag_ids": [],
  "shares": [
    { "person_id": "{{person_id}}", "share_type": "percentage", "share_value": 50 }
  ],
  "notes": "split with Alex",
  "save_mapping": true
}

###

### List processed transactions for a month
GET {{host}}/transactions/processed?year=2026&month=5

###

### Dashboard — summary for one month (calendar mode)
GET {{host}}/dashboard/summary?year=2026&month=5&period_mode=calendar

###

### Dashboard — monthly trend for a year
GET {{host}}/dashboard/monthly-trend?year=2026&period_mode=calendar

###

### Dashboard — split ledger
GET {{host}}/dashboard/split-ledger

###

### Dashboard — same call, financial-year mode (FY 25-26)
GET {{host}}/dashboard/summary?year=2025&month=1&period_mode=fy

###

### Export everything as JSON
GET {{host}}/backup/export

###

### Logout — clears the token cookie
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
